  "extractionNotes": "First paternity part: start printed in the ZUS register (benefit-recipient title row), end truncated on the screenshot. End inferred as day 7: the February payroll row shows 10 of 20 working days not worked, which equals 5 working days of a 7-day part plus 5 working days of sick pay from 2026-02-23. Second part end date: printed as the last day of a benefit row in the ZUS register; the Z-3 gives the same period. The leave application misstates the end year. No full calendar month before the right arose; the employer states the contractual monthly salary 4900.00 in remarks. Z-3 column 6 is the contractual amount, not the actual contribution base, so contributionBase is inferred equal to it. Sick-pay amounts in the register do not match a 13.71% deduction (employer-side computation, not asserted)."
